summary:
The engine (class Engine extends EventEmitter, 2274 lines) owns every root agent's lifecycle and words every reply the person reads. Its deps (policy, commands, workspace, receipt, history) are injected and must never be imported (engine.mjs:4-7). Per-agent state lives in this.runs, a Map from rootId to a run record built in _launch (:1642-1648) or _continueEarlier (:1318-1326): { id, harness, runner, workspace: {path, branch, base}|null, config: Promise, turnSeq, inTurn, deciding, stopped, lastText, receipt, checksDone, waiting, background, backgroundAt, accepted }. Two fields are added later: folderRemoved and earlierSpend. The AgentView carries only the workspace path (agent.created :1651), so branch and base exist only on the run record and in history records. Agents restored from history (earlier: true) have no run at all: their {path, branch|null, base|null} is earlierRecs.get(id).workspace. Every view change goes through _apply (:399). It holds the held-request invariant and calls history.schedule() for HISTORY_KINDS (:40-41, :406).

When a turn ends, _decide (:545) builds the receipt:
- diffStats({path, base}) gives agent.files;
- checkRules gives agent.rules;
- runChecks (with an AbortController signal) gives agent.checks and a done state.
While this runs, run.receipt and run.deciding mark it in progress, and run.checksDone tracks when checks (even cancelled ones) have really ended. _cancelReceipt (:671) aborts it on turn start, on a message the agent took, on stop and on shutdown. During the receipt the view stays working (ACTIVE), but a not-ACTIVE root can still have a live idle Claude process, background commands it was allowed to leave running, and checks still ending.

Confirm cards live in this.confirms (id from hex(6), expire after confirmTtlMs = 10 min). Three functions make them: _proposeStart (:1956), _proposeIntent (:2010, for stop or say found without the agent's name) and _proposeForget (:1370). command() (:1787) settles only the card whose id the page sends (_shownConfirm :1839). On words it does not understand it keeps the card and words a near miss with confirmVerb (:103). Any other command withdraws the card without a notice. _confirm (:2037) branches by kind (forget, stop/say), and anything else falls through to the launch path, which reads c.tasks.

Public wrappers (answer, say, stop, confirm, command) return { ok?, reply, confirm?, focusId?, agentIds? } and post the reply as a notice, except when a confirm comes back. History runs in live mode only:
- _openHistory restores records as earlier views;
- _historyRecords (:1265) is the write source: earlier records go out unchanged, and this run's roots are rebuilt via recordOf with run.folderRemoved ? null : run.workspace;
- _forgetEarlier calls history.forget + store.remove + history.save().

shutdown() (:258) runs in this order: drop later decisions, deny held hooks, wait for launches under way (_launching), stop runners and checks, mark active roots stopped, tidy, close history. The tidy calls _removeUnchanged (:1688: removeWorkspace with onlyIfUnchanged, base and deleteBranch) for every run with a workspace that is not folderRemoved and has no live runner. keptFolders() (:321) lists the rest. Nothing today merges or deletes work: ARCHITECTURE.md:103 says 'the page offers no merge'. snapshot() (:2259) exposes repo {name, head, branch|null, dirty}. That comes from this.repoInfo, which _refreshRepo updates fire-and-forget every 15 s, and the page receives repo only inside a snapshot (on connect, and on store 'removed').

Merge and discard fit best as new confirm kinds on the forget pattern: propose in _runIntent, return a card, add a branch in _confirm before the launch fall-through, then run an executor. They also need:
- an in-flight guard and shutdown wait, mirroring _resuming and _launching;
- one engine-wide lock;
- all checks repeated at yes time;
- a new event, view field and history field to record the outcome.
The diff query should be read-only and reuse diffStats with the same {path, base} as the receipt. Baseline: engine.test.mjs plus history.test.mjs is 138/138 passing with node on PATH. history.test.mjs:569 fails without it, because the fake claude starts with #!/usr/bin/env node.

keyFacts.fact:
_sendTo is the one path that wakes an agent:
- refuses while shutting down;
- sends earlier roots to _continueEarlier;
- clears run.stopped and this.stopped, then runner.send;
- on success cancels the receipt and moves an ENDED root to working.
It has no busy check and no folder-exists check.

_continueEarlier:
- refuses while _shuttingDown, when the record is gone, or when _resuming already has the agent;
- re-checks _canContinue (harness, sessionId, workspace, a directory with .git, sessionExists !== false) and calls store.markContinue on failure;
- on success applies EV.RESUMED + working with a fresh budget.

removeWorkspace:
- only acts on folders git lists as worktrees, never the main folder;
- onlyIfUnchanged (needs base): removes only when HEAD equals base, status --ignored --untracked-files=all is empty and a non-force remove succeeds, then runs update-ref -d on the branch at base;
- without it: worktree remove --force, then branch -D (workbench/ branches only);
- a folder that is no longer listed: prune, return {removed:false}, and leave the branch.

Lid buttons today:
- done: Looks good + Ask for a change (in 'more', a quiet 'What changed?' lists the files);
- earlier: Continue (when canContinue) + Forget (posts /api/command 'forget it' with focusId);
- failed: Try again / Dismiss;
- stopped: Continue / Dismiss.

Test harness in engine.test.mjs:
- live() builds a Store, fakeAdapter claude/codex, fakeDeps and FakeMachines with options { permissionTimeoutMs:5000, tickMs:10_000_000, helperWaitMs:60, exitGraceMs:20 }; demo() uses FakeSim;
- started(t, opts) returns { v, id, runner }, and runner.emit({kind: EV.TURN, …}) drives turns;
- settled(p), until(fn) and gate() hold or poll async work;
- every test ends with engine.shutdown().

extensionPoints.how:
1. Refuse with a plain reply when:
   - it is not live mode;
   - the root is ACTIVE, or run.inTurn, run.deciding or run.receipt is set;
   - this._busy or this._resuming has it;
   - it has no folder.
2. Refresh the repo now: await deps.workspace.prepareRepo(repoInfo.root) and set this.repoInfo. Do not use the fire-and-forget _refreshRepo.
3. Refuse when the branch is null.
4. Run diffStats fresh for the detail.
5. Sentence: a question naming the agent and the branch, e.g. 'Bring Fix login redirect’s work into “main”?'.
6. Detail, short and most important first:
   - counts;
   - check and rule status ('A check failed: “unit tests”.', 'Nothing checked its work.', broken rules);
   - sensitive files (workbench.json, .claude/, .mcp.json);
   - the person's own changes ('Your 2 uncommitted changes stay as they are.').
7. Store { id: hex(6), kind:'merge', agentIds:[v.id], sentence, detail, createdAt: this.now(), seen: { turns: v.turns, stateSince: v.stateSince, workSig, into: branch, intoHead: head } } in this.confirms.
8. Return { reply: sentence, confirm: { id, sentence, detail } }; command() then posts no notice.

For a design that first merges the person's branch into the agent's folder (conflicts stay there, not in the person's checkout), re-run the declared checks in the agent's folder with the same parts:
- run.receipt = { ctl: new AbortController() }, run.deciding = true;
- await run.checksDone before runChecks, and track run.checksDone;
- stale() checks after every await;
- EV.CHECKS updates.
It must stay cancellable by _cancelReceipt and visible to shutdown. A conflict can go to the agent as a follow-up through _sendTo, which resumes a done, stopped or earlier agent.

1. Add to fakeDeps.workspace: mergeWorkspace, diffText and a branch delete, each pushing to calls.* and able to wait on a gate().
2. Cover:
   - a follow-up during a merge is refused;
