rulesToHonour:
A yes or no settles only the card whose id the page sends:
- never 'the newest';
- an unknown or expired id answers GONE;
- any other command withdraws the shown card;
- words not understood keep it, with 'I did not catch that. Say “do it” to <verb>, or “cancel”.';
- cards run out after 10 minutes;
- a card the page drops is withdrawn by POST /api/confirm/<id> {go:false}.

Agent folders and workbench/ branches are the only copy of the work:
- nothing removes them while they may hold work, except an explicit, confirmed discard;
- the shutdown tidy only removes with onlyIfUnchanged and a base;
- a runner that will not stop keeps its folder;
- a folder that cannot go is listed in keptFolders, never left unmentioned.

ARCHITECTURE.md is the contract ('Where code and this document disagree, fix one of them'). Update:
- :103 ('the page offers no merge');
- the Engine API block :267-297;
- the confirm rules :300-307;
- the earlier-agent section :105-112;
- the HTTP table :442-453;
- the answers table :556-569;
- History :405-414.

Tests:
- node:test and node:assert/strict, in test/<module>.test.mjs, owned with the module;
- no network, never a real claude or codex: use the fakes and fixtures;
- engine tests end with shutdown(), keep the tick off (tickMs: 10_000_000), and drive time with options.now or engine.tick(ts).

risks:
The engine treats any card it does not know as a launch:
- confirmVerb words a new kind as 'start it';
- _confirm's fall-through reads c.tasks.length, so a merge or discard card not handled before :2055 throws a TypeError (the generic reply from command(), HTTP 500 from /api/confirm).

Parser traps, all checked with the real parser:
- on any card other than stop/say, 'start it' and 'launch it' are a yes;
- 'forget it' and 'stop' are a no;
- 'merge it' and 'discard it' are not understood, and the near miss would say 'to start it';
- with no card, 'merge search cleanup' and 'delete search cleanup' become launch cards for a new agent.

State is not liveness. A done root can still have:
- a live idle Claude process;
- background commands it was allowed to leave running, writing in its folder;
- cancelled checks still ending (run.checksDone);
- a new turn Claude Code starts by itself when background work ends.
A merge or discard gated on state alone races file writes. Quiesce first (_closeIdle, await checksDone) and hold a busy flag that _sendTo, _continueEarlier, _stop and forget respect.

Stale repo facts:
- repoInfo refreshes every 15 s, and the page sees repo only in snapshots;
- a card can be 10 minutes old;
- the person may have switched branches, committed, started a rebase or detached HEAD meanwhile.
Re-check inside the git operation at the moment of landing; the card's wording only informs.

Dogfooding on Workbench's own repo:
- the server serves ui/ and src/shared/ live from the program folder, so landing into the checkout Workbench runs from changes the page on reload while the engine in memory runs old code;
- run Workbench from a separate checkout, or restart after landing;
- the repo root is /Users/nkov47/IDE, so worktrees copy the whole repo, workbench.json must sit at the root (none exists), and checks need node on PATH.

Claude Code 2.1.322 versus the verified 2.1.221:
- _withEarlierSpend adds the earlier spend to every usage 'set' of a continued run, so spend is counted twice if 2.1.322 restores totals on --resume (ARCHITECTURE.md:109);
- the self-started turn after background work was only read from 2.1.221's code, never recorded;
- the hook exit-2 blocking was verified on 2.1.221 only.
